      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KEVIN (2) is race fit and comes quickly back from a wide-run Class 2 sixth at Coonamble, with the 800m his only real unknown. DENMAN FORCE (3) brings BM66 form, a proven wet-track record and the inside draw after covering ground at Dubbo, so he has the right credentials to rebound. DIVINE SINNER (4) was better than the finishing position at this venue first-up after racing wide and losing a plate, though his unplaced 800m record keeps him more in the place mix than as a clear winning threat. CHICKEN LEGS (5) was out of the money two runs back then again missed the frame last start over 1000m at Dubbo, finishing 11th. Has the ability to improve sharply. SWEDISH GLITTER (7) has been in the market at her last couple of starts since resuming but hasn't made an impression, last start running sixth at Come By Chance. Looks one for the minors.",
